#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# number_decompose

#% text
# `number_decompose(x, [u1, u2, ..., un])` writes `x` as counts of the units `u1`, ..., `u(n-1)` taken greedily, followed by the remainder in units of `un`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The counts are integers truncated toward zero, so negative `x` gives negative counts.

#% item
# The remainder is left exact when `x` is exact.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
number_decompose(100000, [86400, 3600, 60, 1])
#% output
#= [1, 3, 46, 40]

#% cell
number_decompose(99, [10, 5, 2, 1])
#% output
#= [9, 1, 2, 0]

#% cell
number_decompose(-99, [10, 5, 2, 1])
#% output
#= [-9, -1, -2, 0]

#% cell
number_decompose(99/2, [10, 5, 2, 1])
#% output
#= [4, 1, 2, 1/2]

#% cell
number_decompose(10*pi, [e, 1])
#% output
#= [11, -11*e + 10*pi]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `integer_digits`, `quotient`
